Yes.\n\nSW-1 single: 2→20g,1g; 3→20,1; 5→40,2; 6→40,2; 10→100,5; 15→100,5; 20→200,10; 30→200,10. Yes.\n\nDual SW-1: Max 1/2, Min 10, e 0.5/1; 1.5/3, 10, 0.5/1; 2.5/5, 20, 1/2; 3/6, 20, 1/2; 4/10, 40, 2/5; 6/15, 40, 2/5; 10/20, 100, 5/10; 15/30, 100, 5/10. Yes.\n\nDual ED: 1.5/3, 10, 0.5/1; 3/6, 20, 1/2; 6/15, 40, 2/5; 15/30, 100, 5/10. Yes.\n\nDual ER PLUS: 3/6, 20, 1/2; 6/15, 40, 2/5; 15/30, 100, 5/10. Yes.\n\nDual ER JR: 3/6, 20, 1/2; 6/15, 40, 2/5; 15/30, 100, 5/10. Yes.\n\nDual PW-II: 1/2, 10, 0.5/1; 2.5/5, 20, 1/2; 4/10, 40, 2/5. Yes.\n\nSingle ER PLUS: 6→40,2; 15→100,5; 30→200,10. Yes.\n\nSingle ER JR: 6→40,2; 15→100,5; 30→200,10. Yes.\nSingle PW-II: 2→20,1; 5→40,2; 10→100,5. Yes.\n\nFor dual interval min values — the Min column: is Min for the smaller interval? Table just gives one Min per variant. Keep as-is.\n\nNow output. I'll write compact JSON.\n\nAlso include \"alternatives\": null in components? Schema optional. I'll omit alternatives (null) — include only meaningful fields. Actually schema lists alternatives (\"OR\"|\"AND\"|null). I'll set null explicitly. Fine.\n\nLet me draft final JSON:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R76/1992-GB1-10.04\",\n    \"project_number\": \"T1128/0107\",\n    \"page_total\": 4,\n    \"member_state\": \"United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland\",\n    \"date_issued\": \"2014-05-19\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"National Measurement Office\",\n    \"address_lines\": [\"Stanton Avenue\", \"Teddington\", \"TW11 0JZ\", \"United Kingdom\"],\n    \"person_responsible\": \"Paul Dixon\",\n    \"person_title\": \"Director, Product Certification\",\n    \"phone\": \"+44 (0)20 8943 7272\",\n    \"website\": \"www.gov.uk/nmo\"\n  },\n  \"applicants\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"CAS Corporation\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\"#262, Geurugogae-ro\", \"Gwangjeok-myeon\", \"Yangju-si\", \"Gyeonggi-do\", \"Republic of Korea\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"manufacturers\": [\n    {\"name\": \"CAS Corporation\", \"address_lines\": [\"#262, Geurugogae-ro\", \"Gwangjeok-myeon\", \"Yangju-si\", \"Gyeonggi-do\", \"Republic of Korea\"]},\n    {\"name\": \"Shanghai CAS Electronics Co., Ltd\", \"address_lines\": [\"Maixinroad 448\", \"Xinqiaozhen\", \"Songjiangqu\", \"Shanghai\", \"China\"]},\n    {\"name\": \"CAS Elektronik San. Tic. A.S.\", \"address_lines\": [\"Yukari Dudulu, Bostancı Cad. Mevdudi Sokak No: 34\", \"Umraniye-Istanbul\", \"Turkey\"]},\n    {\"name\": \"CAS (Zhejiang) Electronics Co., Ltd\", \"address_lines\": [\"99# Changjiang Road\", \"Jiashan County\", \"Zhejiang Province\", \"China\"]}\n  ],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Non-automatic weighing instrument\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"SW Series\", \"ED\", \"ER PLUS\", \"ER PLUS-M\", \"SW-1\", \"SW-1S\", \"SW-1C\", \"SW-1W\", \"SW-1LR\", \"SW-1WR\", \"ER JR\", \"PW-II\"],\n    \"module_designation\": null,\n    \"description\": \"...\"\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {\n    \"family_name\": \"SW Series\",\n    \"models\": [42 entries]\n  },\n  \"components\": [\n    {\"role\": \"load cell\", \"type_designations\": [\"SW\"], \"alternatives\": null, \"characteristics\": {\"manufacturer\": \"CAS\"}}\n  ],\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"type_level\": {\n      \"accuracy_class\": {\"value\": \"III\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []},\n      \"temperature_range\": {\"value\": {\"min\": -10, \"max\": 40}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\", \"unit_id\": \"u:degree_Celsius\", \"footnote_markers\": []},\n      \"power_supply_type\": {\"value\": \"DC\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []},\n      \"initial_zero_setting_range_of_max\": {\"value\": {\"min\": null, \"max\": 20}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\", \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []},\n      \"semi_automatic_zero_setting_range_of_max\": {\"value\": {\"min\": null, \"max\": 4}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\", \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []},\n      \"zero_tracking_range_of_max\": {\"value\": {\"min\": null, \"max\": 4}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\", \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []}\n    },\n    \"model_level\": [3 big entries],\n    \"config_level\": [\n      power supply voltage,\n      battery option,\n      subtractive tare\n    ]\n  },\n  \"matrix_tables\": [6],\n  \"recommendation\": {\"id\": \"R76\", \"edition\": 1992, \"amendment\": null, \"accuracy_classes\": [\"III\"]},\n  \"test_reports\": [{\"id\": \"P00945\", \"pages\": 24, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"}],\n  \"revision_history\": [...4...]\n}\n\nWait, \"power_supply_type\": \"DC\" — but the instrument is \"mains or battery-operated\". The mains adaptor supplies 12/9 V DC. I'll keep power_supply_type \"DC\" as it's supported by text.\n\nHmm, one nuance: initial zero setting \"≤ 20% of Max\" — value 20 with unit \"%\". Fine.\n\nFor the description, write:\n\n\"Class III, mains or battery-operated, self-indicating, non-automatic weighing instruments designated SW Series, comprising the ED, ER PLUS, ER PLUS-M, SW-1, ER JR and PW-II models and their variants. Steel construction with operator's keypad, stainless steel load receptor, level indicator, and operator and customer display. Devices: initial zero setting device, semi-automatic zero setting device, zero tracking device, zero indicator, net indicator, semi-automatic subtractive tare balancing device, gravity compensation, and check weighing and weighing unstable samples modes (SW-1S, SW-1C, SW-1W, SW-1LR, SW-1WR, ER JR, PW-II and ED models only). Load cell: CAS load cell, model SW. Sealing: access to the load cell and calibration switch is prevented by sealing the enclosure using a wire-and-seal or tamper-evident sticker.\"\n\nConfig level entries:\n\n{\n  \"attribute\": \"power_supply_voltage\",\n  \"axis\": \"model group\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"ED, ER PLUS, ER PLUS M, SW-1S, SW-1C, SW-1W, SW-1LR, SW-1WR, ER JR\", \"value\": 12, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"PW-II\", \"value\