terval Max 5 kg\", \"value\": 5},\n{\"model\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR single-interval Max 6 kg\", \"value\": 6},\n{\"model\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR single-interval Max 10 kg\", \"value\": 10},\n{\"model\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR single-interval Max 15 kg\", \"value\": 15},\n{\"model\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR single-interval Max 20 kg\", \"value\": 20},\n{\"model\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR single-interval Max 30 kg\", \"value\": 30},\n{\"model\": \"ER JR single-interval Max 6 kg\", \"value\": 6},\n{\"model\": \"ER JR single-interval Max 15 kg\", \"value\": 15},\n{\"model\": \"ER JR single-interval Max 30 kg\", \"value\": 30},\n{\"model\": \"PW-II single-interval Max 2 kg\", \"value\": 2},\n{\"model\": \"PW-II single-interval Max 5 kg\", \"value\": 5},\n{\"model\": \"PW-II single-interval Max 10 kg\", \"value\": 10},\n{\"model\": \"ED dual-interval Max 1.5/3 kg\", \"value\": \"1.5/3\"},\n{\"model\": \"ED dual-interval Max 3/6 kg\", \"value\": \"3/6\"},\n{\"model\": \"ED dual-interval Max 6/15 kg\", \"value\": \"6/15\"},\n{\"model\": \"ED dual-interval Max 15/30 kg\", \"value\": \"15/30\"},\n{\"model\": \"ER PLUS/ER PLUS M dual-interval Max 3/6 kg\", \"value\": \"3/6\"},\n{\"model\": \"ER PLUS/ER PLUS M dual-interval Max 6/15 kg\", \"value\": \"6/15\"},\n{\"model\": \"ER PLUS/ER PLUS M dual-interval Max 15/30 kg\", \"value\": \"15/30\"},\n{\"model\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR dual-interval Max 1/2 kg\", \"value\": \"1/2\"},\n{\"model\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR dual-interval Max 1.5/3 kg\", \"value\": \"1.5/3\"},\n{\"model\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR dual-interval Max 2.5/5 kg\", \"value\": \"2.5/5\"},\n{\"model\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR dual-interval Max 3/6 kg\", \"value\": \"3/6\"},\n{\"model\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR dual-interval Max 4/10 kg\", \"value\": \"4/10\"},\n{\"model\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR dual-interval Max 6/15 kg\", \"value\": \"6/15\"},\n{\"model\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR dual-interval Max 10/20 kg\", \"value\": \"10/20\"},\n{\"model\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR dual-interval Max 15/30 kg\", \"value\": \"15/30\"},\n{\"model\": \"ER JR dual-interval Max 3/6 kg\", \"value\": \"3/6\"},\n{\"model\": \"ER JR dual-interval Max 6/15 kg\", \"value\": \"6/15\"},\n{\"model\": \"ER JR dual-interval Max 15/30 kg\", \"value\": \"15/30\"},\n{\"model\": \"PW-II dual-interval Max 1/2 kg\", \"value\": \"1/2\"},\n{\"model\": \"PW-II dual-interval Max 2.5/5 kg\", \"value\": \"2.5/5\"},\n{\"model\": \"PW-II dual-interval Max 4/10 kg\", \"value\": \"4/10\"}\n]\n\nHmm — for dual-interval, is value \"1.5/3\" good, or should I split into max1/max2 attributes? Strings fine, and matrix table shows strings too.\n\nAttribute 2: minimum_capacity (Min), unit \"g\":\nSingle values in same model order:\n20,40,100,200 (ED); 40,100,200 (ERM); 20,20,40,40,100,100,200,200 (SW1); 40,100,200 (ERJR); 20,40,100 (PW-II)\nDual: 10,20,40,100 (ED); 20,40,100 (ERM); 10,10,20,20,40,40,100,100 (SW1); 20,40,100 (ERJR); 10,20,40 (PW-II)\n\nAttribute 3: verification_scale_interval (e), unit \"g\":\nSingle: 1,2,5,10; 2,5,10; 1,1,2,2,5,5,10,10; 2,5,10; 1,2,5\nDual strings: \"0.5/1\",\"1/2\",\"2/5\",\"5/10\"; \"1/2\",\"2/5\",\"5/10\"; \"0.5/1\",\"0.5/1\",\"1/2\",\"1/2\",\"2/5\",\"2/5\",\"5/10\",\"5/10\"; \"1/2\",\"2/5\",\"5/10\"; \"0.5/1\",\"1/2\",\"2/5\"\n\nOK. This will be long but let's write it all out. Also models[] 42 entries with attributes {interval_type}.\n\nLet me think about whether including \"attributes\": {\"interval_type\": \"...\"} in models is needed given model_id contains it. It's fine, adds clarity. I'll include.\n\nmatrix_tables details — 6 entries:\n\n1. name: \"Single-interval instruments — ED and ER PLUS / ER PLUS M\"\n   columns: [\"model\", \"max\", \"min\", \"e\"]\n   column_units: [null, \"kg\", \"g\", \"g\"]\n   rows: 7 rows as above.\n   description: \"Maximum (Max), minimum (Min) load and verification scale interval (e) for single-interval ED and ER PLUS / ER PLUS M variants.\"\n   footnotes: []\n\n2. name: \"Single-interval instruments — SW-1S, SW-1C, SW-1W, SW-1LR, SW-1WR\"\n   rows: 8.\n\n3. name: \"Single-interval instruments — ER JR and PW-II\"\n   rows: 6.\n\n4. name: \"Dual-interval instruments — ED and ER PLUS / ER PLUS M\"\n   columns [\"model\", \"max_max1_max2\", ...]? For dual, max values are \"Max₁ / Max₂\". Column names: \"max1_max2\"? I'll keep \"max\", \"min\", \"e\" and note in description that dual columns give Max1/Max2 and e1/e2. Add description: \"Dual-interval variants: Max and e are given as Max1/Max2 and e1/e2.\"\n   rows with strings \"1.5 / 3\" etc.\n\n5. name: \"Dual-interval instruments — SW-1S, SW-1C, SW-1W, SW-1LR, SW-1WR\", rows 8.\n\n6. name: \"Dual-interval instruments — ER JR and PW-II\", rows 6.\n\nOK. Now finalize revision_history changes text.\n\nAlso should certificate include \"revision\": \"3\"? Schema doesn't have it; revision_history covers. Skip. Hmm — but useful. Rule 8 says don't fabricate fields — adding fields not in schema is risky; revision_history with rev 3 dated 19 May 2014 captures it.\n\nscheme: I'll include \"scheme\": null? Schema says (A|B). Omit entirely. Actually maybe add nothing.\n\nLet me now also double check address of applicant: \"#262, Geurugogae-ro\", \"Gwangjeok-myeon\", \"Yangju-si\", \"Gyeonggi-do\", \"Republic of Korea\". Yes.\n\nAlright, compose final JSON. Ensure valid JSON (no trailing commas, escape nothing weird). Use Unicode °C, ³ etc. — JSON supports UTF-8.\n\nOne thing: unit_id for temperature: \"u:degree_Celsius\" — I'm fairly confident of that ID format per rule 3 example. Include it. Others null.\n\nLet me write the models array (42):\n\n{\"model_id\": \"ED single-interval Max 3 kg\", \"attributes\": {\"interval_type\": \"single-interval\"}},\n{\"model_id\": \"ED single-interval Max 6 kg\", ...},\n{\"model_id\": \"ED single-interval Max 15 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"ED single-interval Max 30 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"ER PLUS/ER PLUS M single-interval Max 6 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"ER PLUS/ER PLUS M single-interval Max 15 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"ER PLUS/ER PLUS M single-interval Max 30 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR single-interval Max 2 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR single-interval Max 3 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR single-interval Max 5 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR single-interval Max 6 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR single-interval Max 10 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR single-interval Max 15 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR single-interval Max 20 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"SW-1S/SW-1C/SW-1W/SW-1LR/SW-1WR single-interval Max 30 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"ER JR single-interval Max 6 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"ER JR single-interval Max 15 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"ER JR single-interval Max 30 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"PW-II single-interval Max 2 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"PW-II single-interval Max 5 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"PW-II single-interval Max 10 kg\"},\n{\"model_id\": \"ED dual-interval Max 1.5/3 kg\", \"attributes\": {\"interval_type\": \"dual-interval\"}},\n... etc.\n\nEach with attributes {\"interval_type\": \"single-interval\"} or \"dual-interval\".\n\nI think this is complete. Write final JSON now. Keep it as one object, minified-ish but readable. I'll produce with indentation for readability but it must parse — indentation is fine.",
